From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:46:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] RD Flow 64: pixel-space palette-pointer model

Retro Diffusion's RD Flow 64 (271M, released 2026-11-24): an hourglass flow transformer over a 64x64 OKLab + alpha
grid (8x8 window attention at 64 and 32, a 16x16 core attending jointly over registers, caption, palette and image),
conditioned on the first 27 layers of Qwen3-VL-4B, with a palette-pointer head. It has no VAE and its own sampler
(16 Euler x-prediction steps, guidance over t <= 0.9, palette extraction at t = 0.6, pointer from 0.35, commit of
confident pixels from 0.55), so generate_image branches to pipeline/rd_flow.cpp, which returns 64x64 RGBA directly.

New request fields palette (--palette, "palette") and opaque_background (--opaque-background,
"opaque_background"). Network calls run one image each; dropped text and unused palette slots are left out
instead of masked, and weights stay F32 (the reference warns its activations overflow F16).

Checked against the reference PyTorch pipeline (fp32, --rng cpu, same caption and seed): a locked palette gives a
pixel-identical image (CLI and sd-server), the model-chosen palette 91% identical pixels with the same mask.
